    "reason": "The changelog line [ev-3cb4e124106a] and the PR description [ev-614ff545d18e] only say that profiling integration was added to tracing instrumentation so a profile can be captured for a single request. Neither names a config key or flag, a default, or whether this is on by default or opt-in. The changed-files list [ev-78902933dc8d] shows edits to pkg/tracing/config.go and cmd/loki/main.go and a vendored dskit spanprofiler. That hints at a new tracing config option, but the key and its default are not shown. Without them, no one can write a typed subject or change, say which environments are exposed (for example, only those with tracing enabled), or say what happens to an operator who does nothing. The pkg/tracing/config.go diff or the documentation added for this change is needed.",
